==English==

===Etymology===
{{etystub}}

The unit of measure sense is from that quantity's often being the amount a person must drink if taking a do-over in a drinking game.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# [[mulligan stew#English|Mulligan stew]].
# {{rfd-redundant|topic=golf}} {{golf}} An unpenalized chance to re-take a stroke that went awry.
#: ''If you lose your drive in the water, take a '''mulligan''' and try again.''
# A second [[chance]].
#: ''Don't do poorly in your first interview; you won't get a '''mulligan'''.''
# {{informal}} A unit of measure equal to 62.5 [[milliliter]]s, or 2.5 shots, of alcohol.
#: ''Tom couldn't handle the shot of tequila, so he had to do a '''mulligan''' of port.''

